⚠️ NOTHING IN THE APP LINKS HERE ANY MORE, as of 2026-08-31. Findings used to
end with a line naming one of these folders. In the shipped app that line was
plain yellow text that could not be clicked, pointing at documents that are not
bundled — and which, opened, turn out to be enterprise runbooks about Active
Directory and HashiCorp Vault rather than anything a person with a key in a chat
log can use. Tony, on seeing it: "they point nowhere and are meaningless."

The remediation steps now live in `mac/Sources/ProtectCore/NextSteps.swift`,
written for the reader the app actually has, with the vendor's own key page as a
button. These files stayed because they are decent background reading for
somebody working on the rules — but by the standard set in the next paragraph
they are now ballast, and whether they stay is Tony's call, not an agent's.

⚠️ FOUR OF 818, DELIBERATELY. The upstream library covers the whole security
domain, including offensive techniques (extracting credentials from memory,
abusing DPAPI) that have no place in a defensive scanner. Only the remediation
guidance matching a rule Protect actually implements is vendored, so every file
here is reachable from a finding rather than sitting in the repo as ballast.

